+# What a workout is
+
+> **Draft for the user to edit.** TRAINER.md: *a human writes the methodology*. Every number below is a proposal drafted from the literature listed at the end. None of it is yours until you have edited it. Lines marked **Decide** have no default that is not a guess about you.
+
+The planner reads this as **criteria, not rules**. Under ADR-0001 the engine never prescribes method, and the planner charter leaves structure, rest, rounds and amounts to the model. Nothing here is checked by the validator, and nothing here should be: a plan that departs from it does so with a reason.
+
+## Decisions only you can make
+
+| | proposal | Decide |
+|---|---|---|
+| primary goal | muscle and strength on the main patterns (TRAINER.md, 8-week criterion 2) | is size or strength first? |
+| hard sets per muscle per cycle | 10-20 | where in the band you start |
+| proximity to failure | 1-3 reps in reserve on working sets | whether you ever go to failure, and on what |
+| circuits | conditioning only, never a way to fit exercises in | whether you want conditioning at all |
+
+## A working set
+
+- **A set that ends 1-3 reps short of failure.** Warm-up and technique sets are not working sets and do not count toward volume. *(Refalo 2023)*
+- **Any load from about 6 to 30 reps builds muscle**, if the set is close to failure. Heavier ranges (3-6) build more maximal strength. *(Schoenfeld 2017b)*
+- **With body weight and bands, reps are the dial.** A set of 8 push-ups that leaves 15 in reserve is not a working set. Pick the variant that makes the target reps hard: harder via `variant_of`, easier via `regression_of`. *(Calatayud 2015: band push-ups matched bench press for strength at equal effort)*
+
+## How much
+
+| per | proposal | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| muscle, per cycle | 10-20 hard sets | Schoenfeld 2017a |
+| muscle, per workout | up to about 6-8 hard sets; past that, add a workout, not sets | Iversen 2021 |
+| group, per workout | 2-3 exercises, 2-4 sets each | follows from the two rows above |
+
+**Two exercises for one group earn their place by differing**: in movement pattern, in primary muscle, or in the position that loads the muscle (stretched vs shortened). Four push-up variants are one exercise four times.
+
+## Structure
+
+| shape | reach for it when | avoid it when |
+|---|---|---|
+| **straight sets** | the main compound of the workout; anything heavy; anything needing full recovery between sets | — default |
+| **superset** | two exercises that do not compete: antagonists (push/pull, biceps/triceps) or distant groups. Saves time at little cost to performance. *(Robbins 2010; Weakley 2017)* | both exercises load the same muscle: the second set starts tired, reps fall |
+| **circuit** | conditioning, or a short workout of light, non-competing exercises | it is being used to fit more exercises of one group into the time |
+
+**More time goes into sets and rest, not into more exercises.** A circuit is the cheapest shape the engine costs (three rests instead of fifteen); cheap is a reason to check it, not to choose it.
+
+**Less time cuts exercises, not working sets.** Keep the main compound per group, drop the accessories, pair what does not compete. *(Iversen 2021)*
+
+## Rest
+
+| work | proposal | source |
+|---|---|---|
+| heavy compound, 3-6 reps | 2-3 min | Grgic 2018 |
+| compound, 6-15 reps | 90-120 s, at least | Schoenfeld 2016 |
+| isolation | 60-90 s | ACSM 2009 |
+| superset of non-competing exercises | the rest of the more demanding one, taken after the pair | Robbins 2010 |
+
+Short rest does not make a set harder in a useful way; it makes the next one worse. These are the bands `PLANNING` already quotes, with the reason attached.
+
+## Order
+
+1. The most demanding compound first, for the group the workout is for. *(Simão 2012)*
+2. Then the other compounds, then isolation.
+3. Core and timed work last, unless it is the workout's point.
+
+## Worked example: chest and arms, 45 min, body weight and bands
+
+What the bot proposed in session 7 against what this document would ask for:
+
+| | proposed | this document |
+|---|---|---|
+| shape | two circuits, nine exercises | straight sets for the main push, then straight sets or one superset |
+| chest | four push-up variants, 8 reps each | one push-up variant hard at 8-12, one band crossover |
+| arms | five triceps exercises | two triceps exercises that differ in position: one overhead, one not |
+| rest | 90 s after a round of five | 90-120 s on the push-up; 60-90 s on the rest |
+| time | 25 of 45 min | the 45, spent on sets |
+
+With body weight and bands the catalog has no biceps strength exercise, only a stretch: arms here means triceps. That is a gap in the data, not something the plan can fix.
+
+## Sources
+
+Not yet checked against the papers by the user. Verify each before relying on it.
